Britain and the Thirteen Colonies, which won independence as the United States of America","x":"The American Revolutionary War (April 19, 1775 – September 3, 1783), also known as the Revolutionary War or American War of Independence or simply the American Revolution, was the armed conflict that comprised the final eight years of the broader American Revolution, in which American Patriot forces organized as the Continental Army and, commanded by George Washington, defeated the British Army. The conflict was fought in North America, the Caribbean, and the Atlantic Ocean. Outcome: American and allied victory; Signing of the United States Declaration of Independence in 1776.; Great Britain would not recognize American independence until signing the Treaty of Paris.; Peace of Paris; End of the First British Empire. Cost: Great Britain cedes generally, all mainland territories east of the Mississippi River, south of the Great Lakes, and north of the Floridas to the United States..","o":"American Revolution","l":[["Wikidata","https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q40949"],["Britannica","https://www.britannica.com/event/American-Revolution"],["avalon.law.yale.edu","http://avalon.law.yale.edu/18th_century/proc1783.asp"],["Journal of the American Revolution","https://allthingsliberty.com/2015/02/indian-patriots-from-eastern-massachusetts-six-perspectives/"],["US National Park Service","https://www.nps.gov/ande/learn/historyculture/pow_synopsis.htm"],["Encyclopaedia Britannica","https://www.britannica.com/event/American-Revolution"],["Library of Congress","https://id.loc.gov/authorities/sh85140139"],["Wikipedia","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Revolutionary_War"]]},{"c":4,"k":3,"t":"Earthquake","w":"3 September 1771","y":1771,"p":"Jamaica: Port Royal,Kingston","l":[["NOAA NCEI","https://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/hazel/view/hazards/earthquake/event-more-info/1409"]]},{"c":1,"k":15,"t":"Tacky's War","w":"7 April 1760 – 1761","y":1760,"p":"Colony of Jamaica","s":"slave revolt in Jamaica"